# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Every dangerous pattern is written BOTH bare and with a leading **/ so the
# exclusion holds regardless of matcher semantics. A bare ".env" excludes only
# the root file under some matchers, which would happily copy src/.env into the
# image; "**/.env" alone is ambiguous about the root. Listing both is free.
#
# NOTE: no "*.sql" pattern. It would risk excluding
# prisma/migrations/*/migration.sql, which the migrator image requires. Database
# dumps are covered by "backups" and "*.dump" instead. The explicit !prisma
# negation at the end is a belt-and-braces guarantee for the migrator.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# dependencies and build output
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# environment files and secrets (both forms, deliberately)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
*.crt
**/*.crt
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*

# version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# tests and test tooling — never needed in any image
tests
**/tests
vitest.config.mts
coverage

# local database data, backups and dumps
backups
pgdata
**/pgdata
*.dump
**/*.dump

# development artifacts and editor state
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
docs

# The migrator image needs prisma/schema.prisma and prisma/migrations/**.
# This negation must remain LAST so nothing above can strip them.
!prisma
